 "about": "Source of comfyui-hive/catalog.json: tools/build.py. A task's template is a ComfyUI workflow template of that version. An input's param is a setting shown on the template's subgraph (its label) or 'node.input' for a template without one. Variants are best first; the page offers the first that fits the GPU: min_vram_gb (as nvidia-smi reports it, so a 24 GB card is 23.99) and min_compute (CUDA compute capability). replace swaps a file the workflows load for another build in the same folder; set is [node, input, value]. An input of kind loras lets the page add the user's own LoRAs to the task: after lists the model outputs they are chained onto, [node] or [node, \"low\"] for the low-noise model of a pair (which takes a slot's second file); every such input gets the slots and strength limits of loras below; its clip ([node, output] of the text encoder, for a single model) applies each LoRA to the text encoder too (LoraLoader), as SD 1.5 and SDXL LoRAs expect. A model's files puts its own file in place of one the template loads ({template file: {name, url}}), for a model run through another's template (a checkpoint). A task's set is [node, input, value] of the template it always changes; its clip_skip adds a CLIPSetLastLayer of that layer after that CLIP output. A task's like names a task of tasks below that several models share; the task's own keys are added to it, and its defaults ({input: value}) replace those inputs' defaults.",
